## 6. EVERY RECOVERY1 V10 option, independent truth and complete set

Use the actual graph observations above and the frozen original-source
results; do not read or infer an author key.

| Option | Independent truth | Concrete graph/result evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| a | false | Crossing (0,1) and equation {0} match, but the order is reversed. At x=-1, visible C is 10/7 below visible D=2.5; at x=1, C=0.7 is above D=0.4. Both proposed strict intervals are consequently reversed. |
| b | false | Crossing, left/right order and equation are correct, but [0,+infinity) and (-infinity,0] include x=0 in strict inequalities. The common point has C(0)=D(0)=1, so neither strict inequality holds there. |
| c | true | The graph crosses only at (0,1); C is below D on the negative side and above D on the positive side. The report {0}, (0,+infinity), (-infinity,0) matches the frozen complete solutions, with equality excluded from both strict sets. |
| d | false | It swaps the crossing coordinates to (1,0), whereas the actual crossing lies on x=0 at y=1. At x=1, the graph shows separate positive values 0.7 and 0.4, not a crossing. Equation {1} is wrong; (1,+infinity) omits valid greater-than inputs such as x=0.5, and (-infinity,1) includes invalid less-than inputs such as x=0.5. The claimed ordering relative to the false crossing is therefore not a valid global report either. |

Independently complete true set: {c}.
Single-mode cardinality: exactly one true complete claim.
All four option assertions were checked, including correct subclauses of
false options. No author correct set or rationale was disclosed.

